1
00:00:00,292 --> 00:00:03,003
Patricia, something happened
to your mom.

2
00:00:03,003 --> 00:00:04,296
Mama!

3
00:00:04,296 --> 00:00:05,715
Whoo!

4
00:00:05,715 --> 00:00:07,550
I won't fall for your act.

5
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:09,218
And whatever your plan is,

6
00:00:09,218 --> 00:00:11,929
I will make sure
you don't succeed!

7
00:00:11,929 --> 00:00:14,306
Mama!

8
00:00:14,306 --> 00:00:16,809
Let's work together
to save La Familia.

9
00:00:16,809 --> 00:00:18,352
Save or destroy?

10
00:00:18,352 --> 00:00:21,105
There's a lot you don't know
about what happened.

11
00:00:21,105 --> 00:00:23,691
I choose
to believe you, Patricia.

12
00:00:23,691 --> 00:00:25,484
You are not your mistakes.

13
00:00:25,484 --> 00:00:28,237
If we want to outsmart
Sir Ricardo,

14
00:00:28,237 --> 00:00:30,656
we need someone
who can get close to him.

15
00:00:30,656 --> 00:00:32,408
I will approach him.

16
00:00:32,408 --> 00:00:34,243
I will pretend to be his ally.

17
00:00:34,243 --> 00:00:36,871
Sir Ricardo? I was
with Patricia earlier.

18
00:00:36,871 --> 00:00:38,122
Someone called her.

19
00:00:38,122 --> 00:00:39,999
They said they've found
Miss D's body.

20
00:00:39,999 --> 00:00:41,041
She's dead.

21
00:00:42,793 --> 00:00:44,879
Are you Patricia Dela Cruz?

22
00:00:47,089 --> 00:00:48,215
This way, please.

23
00:00:55,723 --> 00:00:56,974
- Enzo.
- Sir Ricardo.

24
00:00:56,974 --> 00:00:58,058
Where's Diana's body?

25
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,602
Over there.
Patricia's already there.

26
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:06,734
Miss, where's my wife?

27
00:01:06,734 --> 00:01:08,944
Sir, we've been waiting for you.

28
00:01:08,944 --> 00:01:09,987
This way.

29
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,993
Where's Diana, Patricia?

30
00:02:45,875 --> 00:02:47,001
Why...

31
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:50,462
Why didn't anyone call me?

32
00:02:51,505 --> 00:02:52,965
Why did they only call you?

33
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:56,802
They said they couldn't
reach you.

34
00:02:56,802 --> 00:03:00,681
They never called me. Why...

35
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:09,398
I'm not the one
you should be asking that.

36
00:03:12,860 --> 00:03:15,154
Why did you decide to
have her cremated right away?

37
00:03:15,154 --> 00:03:16,947
Why didn't you wait for me?

38
00:03:16,947 --> 00:03:21,327
They said Mama's body
was already badly decomposed.

39
00:03:22,578 --> 00:03:25,581
I didn't want people
to see her in that state.

40
00:03:25,581 --> 00:03:26,957
I wouldn't be able to bear it.

41
00:03:30,044 --> 00:03:32,963
What did the autopsy say?

42
00:03:32,963 --> 00:03:34,673
What happened to Diana?

43
00:03:34,673 --> 00:03:36,926
Her body was already in an
advanced state of decomposition

44
00:03:36,926 --> 00:03:38,052
when it was found.

45
00:03:38,636 --> 00:03:41,096
The jewelry and dental structure

46
00:03:41,096 --> 00:03:43,515
were the only things
we could use to identify her.

47
00:03:43,515 --> 00:03:44,850
What was the cause of death?

48
00:03:45,267 --> 00:03:46,435
That's the problem, sir.

49
00:03:46,435 --> 00:03:48,520
The autopsy was inconclusive.

50
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:51,941
Her body was found in the water,
so it decomposed quickly,

51
00:03:52,524 --> 00:03:55,611
and the tissue in her chest
had been washed away.

52
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:59,198
Since there were no marks
left on the bones,

53
00:03:59,198 --> 00:04:03,494
the crime lab couldn't determine
the exact cause of death.

54
00:04:24,848 --> 00:04:26,266
Diana...

55
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:12,980
This shouldn't have happened
to Diana...

56
00:05:17,776 --> 00:05:19,403
Nanny Cora...

57
00:05:21,989 --> 00:05:23,615
She doesn't deserve this...

58
00:05:27,578 --> 00:05:31,749
By the virtue of
the authority vested in me

59
00:05:32,541 --> 00:05:36,045
by the laws of the
Republic of the Philippines,

60
00:05:36,045 --> 00:05:39,089
and in the presence
of your witnesses,

61
00:05:39,089 --> 00:05:43,218
I now pronounce you
husband and wife.

62
00:05:44,178 --> 00:05:46,305
You may now kiss the bride.

63
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:57,066
Ta-da!

64
00:05:57,066 --> 00:06:00,527
The remains of
La Familia CEO Diana Aragon

65
00:06:00,527 --> 00:06:01,987
have been found.

66
00:06:01,987 --> 00:06:04,656
Investigators have yet
to determine

67
00:06:04,656 --> 00:06:06,492
- the cause of death...
- See?

68
00:06:06,492 --> 00:06:09,536
due to the body's advanced
state of decomposition.

69
00:06:09,536 --> 00:06:11,747
- Told you.
- Police have not ruled out

70
00:06:11,747 --> 00:06:13,499
the possibility of an accident

71
00:06:13,499 --> 00:06:17,211
and continue to investigate
whether foul play was involved.

72
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:25,844
Aww...

73
00:06:29,473 --> 00:06:31,558
I'm sorry, Diana...

74
00:06:34,978 --> 00:06:36,563
I'm sorry!

75
00:06:40,275 --> 00:06:42,486
Diana, I'm sorry!

76
00:06:44,279 --> 00:06:47,533
Diana...

77
00:06:49,326 --> 00:06:50,536
Pack them up.

78
00:06:52,121 --> 00:06:53,747
What are you...

79
00:06:53,747 --> 00:06:56,583
Why are you packing up my stuff?
What's this supposed to mean?

80
00:06:56,959 --> 00:06:58,794
I'm sorry, Patricia.

81
00:06:58,794 --> 00:07:01,421
But your designation was
coterminous with Miss D's.

82
00:07:01,421 --> 00:07:03,048
Now that she's gone,

83
00:07:03,048 --> 00:07:05,175
your position
has been dissolved, too.

84
00:07:06,218 --> 00:07:07,386
Take them.

85
00:07:09,388 --> 00:07:10,931
Don't touch it!

86
00:07:10,931 --> 00:07:12,683
Don't touch anything!

87
00:07:13,392 --> 00:07:14,935
I'm sorry, Patricia.

88
00:07:14,935 --> 00:07:19,356
But we were ordered to remove
everything you used here.

89
00:07:19,356 --> 00:07:20,566
Even the table.

90
00:07:20,566 --> 00:07:21,859
You're not taking-- Ouch!

91
00:07:21,859 --> 00:07:23,318
- Let go of me!
- I'm sorry, ma'am.

92
00:07:23,318 --> 00:07:26,321
You're not taking that
out of here! I'm not leaving!

93
00:07:26,321 --> 00:07:27,739
I said let go!

94
00:07:27,739 --> 00:07:28,866
We're just following orders.

95
00:07:28,866 --> 00:07:30,826
Whose orders? Ricardo's?!

96
00:07:30,826 --> 00:07:33,162
Where is he?!
Why won't he face me?!

97
00:07:33,162 --> 00:07:34,705
I know he's behind this!

98
00:07:34,705 --> 00:07:37,040
He can't force me
out of La Familia!

99
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,709
- Ma'am--
- I said let go of me!

100
00:07:38,709 --> 00:07:40,169
Ricardo!

101
00:07:40,169 --> 00:07:42,254
- Let go of me!
- Let's go, ma'am.

102
00:07:42,254 --> 00:07:44,006
I said let go of me!

103
00:07:44,006 --> 00:07:45,632
- I'm sorry, ma'am.
- Let go of me!

104
00:07:45,632 --> 00:07:48,594
You can't do this to me!
Let go of me!

105
00:07:48,594 --> 00:07:49,928
Ricardo!

106
00:07:49,928 --> 00:07:52,055
Let go of me!

107
00:07:52,055 --> 00:07:53,765
I said let go of me!

108
00:07:54,683 --> 00:07:56,685
You're so shameless.

109
00:07:56,685 --> 00:07:58,979
If you think you can
kick me out easily,

110
00:07:58,979 --> 00:08:00,355
you're wrong!

111
00:08:00,939 --> 00:08:02,774
I'm my mother's daughter.

112
00:08:02,774 --> 00:08:05,903
You can't take away my rights
to La Familia!

113
00:08:05,903 --> 00:08:07,487
Let me remind you...

114
00:08:08,322 --> 00:08:09,823
I'm an Aragon.

115
00:08:31,303 --> 00:08:33,222
Shouldn't we be worried?

116
00:08:34,014 --> 00:08:36,433
The employees seem
to be on Patricia's side.

117
00:08:36,808 --> 00:08:38,143
What are they going to do?

118
00:08:38,894 --> 00:08:40,354
Mass resignation?

119
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:42,731
They're not going to do that.

120
00:08:42,731 --> 00:08:45,067
They need their jobs.
Life is hard right now.

121
00:08:46,193 --> 00:08:49,696
What we should be worried about
is the board...

122
00:08:49,696 --> 00:08:50,822
the election...

123
00:08:51,573 --> 00:08:53,533
me becoming CEO.

124
00:08:54,618 --> 00:08:58,247
Diana's last will and testament
will be read soon.

125
00:09:15,013 --> 00:09:16,223
Georgia.

126
00:09:17,891 --> 00:09:19,559
What are you doing here?

127
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,144
You're in touch
with my dad, right?

128
00:09:22,854 --> 00:09:24,106
I want to talk to him.

129
00:09:24,773 --> 00:09:26,942
He hasn't been
answering his phone.

130
00:09:28,485 --> 00:09:30,279
The board is the one
in contact with him.

131
00:09:30,279 --> 00:09:31,655
You can't fool me.

132
00:09:32,030 --> 00:09:33,740
Don't waste my time.

133
00:09:34,533 --> 00:09:35,784
I'm just desperate.

134
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:39,204
I just want to talk
to my dad, so please...

135
00:09:39,204 --> 00:09:41,123
I will do anything.

136
00:09:42,541 --> 00:09:44,001
I'll do whatever you want.

137
00:09:44,001 --> 00:09:46,795
Just please let me contact
my dad.

138
00:09:54,553 --> 00:09:56,179
Where's Patricia?

139
00:09:57,139 --> 00:09:58,223
I don't know.

140
00:09:58,223 --> 00:09:59,933
Maybe she's still
crying her eyes out.

141
00:10:08,692 --> 00:10:10,569
Finally, you're here.

142
00:10:17,993 --> 00:10:19,786
Let's start, Attorney.

143
00:10:20,829 --> 00:10:24,333
Um, before we begin,
I want you to know

144
00:10:25,167 --> 00:10:28,086
that as per Miss D's
strict instructions,

145
00:10:28,086 --> 00:10:33,050
this is the first time I'll open
her last will and testament.

146
00:10:33,050 --> 00:10:36,345
So, I have no idea
what's written here.

147
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:47,189
"I, Diana Aragon Salvador,
Filipino, of legal age,

148
00:10:47,189 --> 00:10:49,441
married to Ricardo Salvador,

149
00:10:49,441 --> 00:10:52,903
being of sound and disposing
mind and memory,

150
00:10:52,903 --> 00:10:57,074
and not acting under duress,
menace, fraud,

151
00:10:57,074 --> 00:10:59,659
or undue influence
from anyone,

152
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:03,497
do hereby declare and
proclaim the instrument

153
00:11:03,497 --> 00:11:05,916
to be my last
will and testament.

154
00:11:05,916 --> 00:11:09,252
To my beloved husband,
Ricardo Salvador,

155
00:11:10,379 --> 00:11:15,467
I give and bequeath 25 percent
of my total general estate

156
00:11:15,467 --> 00:11:18,637
as his lawful share
as my surviving spouse."

157
00:11:18,637 --> 00:11:19,763
Wait.

158
00:11:20,305 --> 00:11:21,765
I thought you had a prenup.

159
00:11:22,265 --> 00:11:23,558
That was the plan.

160
00:11:24,810 --> 00:11:27,270
But before Diana died...

161
00:11:28,563 --> 00:11:30,857
she changed her mind
about the prenup,

162
00:11:30,857 --> 00:11:32,609
so we didn't file it.

163
00:11:32,609 --> 00:11:34,069
That's a lie.

164
00:11:35,445 --> 00:11:36,863
Patricia.

165
00:11:36,863 --> 00:11:39,032
We have a lawyer
here with us.

166
00:11:39,032 --> 00:11:41,660
She'll prove that it's true.

167
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:42,911
Please continue, Attorney.

168
00:11:45,622 --> 00:11:47,916
"To my only beloved daughter,

169
00:11:47,916 --> 00:11:50,419
Patricia Monique Aragon
Dela Cruz,

170
00:11:50,419 --> 00:11:55,590
I give and bequeath 50 percent
of my total general estate

171
00:11:55,590 --> 00:11:58,844
as her lawful share
as my legitimate child."

172
00:12:01,513 --> 00:12:04,057
To my brother,
Teodor Aragon,

173
00:12:04,057 --> 00:12:06,351
and his daughter,
Georgia Aragon,

174
00:12:06,351 --> 00:12:10,939
I give and bequeath
the remaining 25 percent

175
00:12:10,939 --> 00:12:14,276
of my general estate
in equal shares."

176
00:12:14,276 --> 00:12:17,154
However, since they're
both not here,

177
00:12:17,154 --> 00:12:19,781
we will discuss this matter
another time.

178
00:12:22,617 --> 00:12:24,911
And now...

179
00:12:24,911 --> 00:12:29,332
"As to my 25 percent ownership
in corresponding shares

180
00:12:29,332 --> 00:12:31,543
in La Familia Corporation,

181
00:12:31,543 --> 00:12:37,924
I hereby give, bequeath,
and transfer all of said shares

182
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:41,470
exclusively to my
legitimate daughter,

183
00:12:41,470 --> 00:12:44,556
Patricia Monique Aragon
Dela Cruz.

184
00:12:44,556 --> 00:12:48,435
These shares shall be formally
transferred to her name

185
00:12:48,435 --> 00:12:52,063
in accordance with the laws,
corporate by-laws,

186
00:12:52,063 --> 00:12:55,358
and regulations
governing the corporation."

187
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:00,947
How did that happen?
I was her husband.

188
00:13:02,199 --> 00:13:04,868
That's what's written
in Diana's last will.

189
00:13:04,868 --> 00:13:08,038
She made some changes
before your marriage.

190
00:13:08,038 --> 00:13:11,541
If you want to contest the will,
you have the right to do so.

191
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:15,462
After all, you are a compulsory
heir as her husband.

192
00:13:28,558 --> 00:13:30,644
We have a lawyer
here with us.

193
00:13:35,148 --> 00:13:36,483
Thank you, Attorney.

194
00:13:48,453 --> 00:13:50,872
Aah!

195
00:13:55,794 --> 00:13:56,962
Sir?

196
00:13:59,339 --> 00:14:00,715
What happened?

197
00:14:06,846 --> 00:14:10,058
Why didn't you tell me
Diana did that?!

198
00:14:10,058 --> 00:14:11,268
What do you mean?

199
00:14:11,268 --> 00:14:13,436
I don't know what you're
talking about.

200
00:14:13,436 --> 00:14:17,399
Diana gave all her shares
in La Familia to Patricia!

201
00:14:17,399 --> 00:14:19,401
You were her right hand.
How come you didn't know?

202
00:14:20,610 --> 00:14:23,321
There were many things
Miss D didn't tell me.

203
00:14:23,321 --> 00:14:24,864
That's how cautious she was.

204
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:26,783
As she should.

205
00:14:27,492 --> 00:14:29,202
She had every right
to do so!

206
00:14:29,744 --> 00:14:31,871
I want you to keep
an eye on Patricia.

207
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:34,040
Follow her wherever
she goes.

208
00:14:34,624 --> 00:14:37,127
Find out her plans
and every move.

209
00:14:37,127 --> 00:14:38,920
Then, report it to me!

210
00:14:39,379 --> 00:14:40,589
Do you understand?!

211
00:14:41,256 --> 00:14:43,425
Yes, I understand.

212
00:15:03,403 --> 00:15:04,946
As of this quarter,

213
00:15:06,072 --> 00:15:09,826
we need to reduce
unnecessary expenses

214
00:15:09,826 --> 00:15:14,247
and realign the company's
operations.

215
00:15:14,247 --> 00:15:16,625
Mr. and Mrs. Smith
are here

216
00:15:16,625 --> 00:15:18,877
as shareholders
of the company.

217
00:15:18,877 --> 00:15:22,964
Considering this involves
La Familia's future,

218
00:15:22,964 --> 00:15:26,259
my wife and I believe we
have the right to sit here

219
00:15:26,259 --> 00:15:29,012
and see where this is headed.

220
00:15:29,012 --> 00:15:34,059
After all, Burger City's future
is on the line here too.

221
00:15:34,059 --> 00:15:35,685
So...

222
00:15:35,685 --> 00:15:37,062
That is true.

223
00:15:50,158 --> 00:15:52,619
Patricia, what are you
doing here?

224
00:15:56,831 --> 00:15:59,542
I own a large amount of shares
in this company...

225
00:16:01,169 --> 00:16:03,797
so I have the right
to be here.

226
00:16:08,718 --> 00:16:10,512
But this is all corporate talk.

227
00:16:10,512 --> 00:16:12,097
You might not understand it.

228
00:16:12,097 --> 00:16:13,640
Why, Sir Ricardo?

229
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:16,559
Is my presence
making you feel uneasy?

230
00:16:16,559 --> 00:16:18,269
Patricia.

231
00:16:18,311 --> 00:16:22,107
Stop...
Stop forcing yourself here.

232
00:16:22,107 --> 00:16:25,193
We're the ones running
La Familia now.

233
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:28,446
Why are you here, Ma?

234
00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:32,367
I'm part of the board now.

235
00:16:32,951 --> 00:16:36,913
And when we're here,

236
00:16:36,913 --> 00:16:39,582
can you stop calling
me Mama?

237
00:16:40,417 --> 00:16:43,086
It's so unprofessional.

238
00:16:43,086 --> 00:16:45,714
That's Mrs. Smith for you.

239
00:16:46,214 --> 00:16:48,591
You know, Patricia, you might
only get confused.

240
00:16:49,759 --> 00:16:51,386
I mean, what do you know
about all this?

241
00:16:52,011 --> 00:16:53,430
You're not a graduate.

242
00:16:53,430 --> 00:16:57,058
Is that how you're going to
talk to me, Mr. Salvador?

243
00:16:59,144 --> 00:17:00,687
Yes, I'm not a graduate.

244
00:17:01,438 --> 00:17:06,109
But I own the largest share
in this company.

245
00:17:08,111 --> 00:17:10,071
In case you forgot...

246
00:17:11,781 --> 00:17:15,076
my family owns La Familia.

247
00:17:16,244 --> 00:17:19,539
They spent their entire lives
in this company.

248
00:17:20,915 --> 00:17:24,335
You're nothing but a husband.

249
00:17:25,295 --> 00:17:28,381
I'm fighting for my
family's legacy.

250
00:17:29,132 --> 00:17:33,553
And don't ever underestimate
what an Aragon can do.

251
00:17:38,099 --> 00:17:40,435
The annual board election
is coming up.

252
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:47,942
And I'm going to use every
percentage of my shares

253
00:17:47,942 --> 00:17:50,612
to protect La Familia.

254
00:17:52,197 --> 00:17:53,531
Sure.

255
00:17:54,574 --> 00:17:57,243
That is, if someone nominates
or votes for you.

256
00:18:03,166 --> 00:18:04,793
From now on,
it's a numbers game.

257
00:18:04,793 --> 00:18:08,922
You need 51 percent of the votes
to achieve your goal.

258
00:18:08,922 --> 00:18:12,759
What if we take into
consideration the shares

259
00:18:12,759 --> 00:18:16,262
of Mr. Smith and
Ricardo's allies?

260
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:21,851
You're almost equal
in shares.

261
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:25,313
We really need
to convince one of them.

262
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:33,071
It will be hard to convince
Mr. Smith.

263
00:18:33,071 --> 00:18:35,490
Mama won't let me
get close to him,

264
00:18:35,490 --> 00:18:38,618
especially now that
she's on Ricardo's side.

265
00:18:41,454 --> 00:18:42,580
Hey.

266
00:18:45,416 --> 00:18:46,960
We'll give it our best shot.

267
00:18:48,044 --> 00:18:50,129
Okay? One step at a time.

268
00:19:13,695 --> 00:19:14,737
Hello?

269
00:19:14,737 --> 00:19:16,573
This is Ricardo Salvador.

270
00:19:17,115 --> 00:19:18,533
I have a meeting
with Mr. Meneses.

271
00:19:18,533 --> 00:19:19,617
Why isn't he here yet?

272
00:19:19,617 --> 00:19:21,077
I'm sorry, Mister Ricardo.

273
00:19:21,077 --> 00:19:23,162
There's a sudden change
in his schedule.

274
00:19:23,162 --> 00:19:25,123
He won't be able
to meet you anymore.

275
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:28,042
What? Why?

276
00:19:28,042 --> 00:19:31,880
He said he has to go
to another meeting.

277
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:33,840
What meeting?
Who is he meeting with?

278
00:19:34,215 --> 00:19:36,551
Patricia Dela Cruz.

279
00:19:51,065 --> 00:19:53,192
I only agreed to meet with you

280
00:19:53,192 --> 00:19:54,611
because of your mother.

281
00:19:54,611 --> 00:19:58,281
I believed
in Diana's capabilities.

282
00:19:58,281 --> 00:20:02,035
However, I don't think
you have enough experience.

283
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:05,872
I understand, sir.

284
00:20:09,292 --> 00:20:11,586
I may not have
enough experience,

285
00:20:13,129 --> 00:20:16,883
but I'm the one who cares
about La Familia the most.

286
00:20:16,883 --> 00:20:18,384
My mother nurtured this company,

287
00:20:19,469 --> 00:20:24,515
so I won't let all her hard work
be in vain.

288
00:20:24,515 --> 00:20:27,852
I admit that I have my doubts
about Ricardo's actions.

289
00:20:27,852 --> 00:20:31,481
I know Diana would disagree
with what he's doing.

290
00:20:31,481 --> 00:20:35,151
But legacy doesn't keep
a company alive, Patricia.

291
00:20:36,444 --> 00:20:38,029
Leadership does.

292
00:20:41,950 --> 00:20:43,660
What happened?

293
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:46,496
That damn Meneses
stood me up.

294
00:20:46,496 --> 00:20:49,165
How did your call with
the other board members go?

295
00:20:49,165 --> 00:20:50,959
Well, the majority of them
are on your side.

296
00:20:50,959 --> 00:20:52,168
And the rest?

297
00:20:52,835 --> 00:20:54,295
They're not budging,

298
00:20:54,295 --> 00:20:56,297
but you don't have
to worry about them.

299
00:20:57,465 --> 00:20:59,258
- Okay?
- Make sure...

300
00:20:59,258 --> 00:21:01,135
...Patricia doesn't get
any votes.

301
00:21:01,886 --> 00:21:04,263
Okay, darling. Okay.

302
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:06,182
Okay. I'll take care of that.

303
00:21:06,766 --> 00:21:08,643
Okay?

304
00:21:28,705 --> 00:21:30,707
It's empty!
No one's here!

305
00:21:30,707 --> 00:21:31,916
What?

306
00:21:31,916 --> 00:21:33,918
Sir Ricardo won't like this!

307
00:21:39,132 --> 00:21:40,258
Hello, Oliver.

308
00:21:41,426 --> 00:21:43,302
You're right, bestie.

309
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:45,555
That Sir Ricardo of yours
likes to play dirty.

310
00:21:45,555 --> 00:21:47,890
Some men are lurking in front
of your house right now.

311
00:21:47,890 --> 00:21:49,559
I heard them talking.

312
00:21:49,559 --> 00:21:50,935
He sent them.

313
00:21:50,935 --> 00:21:53,396
Okay, I'll call Papa.

314
00:21:53,396 --> 00:21:55,523
I'll tell him
not to come home for now.

315
00:21:56,566 --> 00:21:58,526
Can he stay at your place
for tonight?

316
00:21:58,526 --> 00:21:59,736
Of course.

317
00:21:59,736 --> 00:22:01,696
I've got you.
Take care, bestie.

318
00:22:02,238 --> 00:22:03,740
Thank you, Oliver.

319
00:22:05,825 --> 00:22:08,244
Search the area!
He's probably just hiding!

320
00:22:08,244 --> 00:22:09,245
Copy.

321
00:22:18,504 --> 00:22:19,797
Where's Patricia?

322
00:22:21,257 --> 00:22:23,509
Well, she knows what time
the meeting will start.

323
00:22:23,509 --> 00:22:25,053
She should be here by now.

324
00:22:25,845 --> 00:22:27,972
Are we gonna let
the stockholders wait?

325
00:22:31,309 --> 00:22:33,394
Let us begin the
shareholders' meeting.

326
00:22:37,315 --> 00:22:39,442
Shut the door.
Don't let anyone in.

327
00:22:45,823 --> 00:22:48,451
May I? I'd like to
say a few things.

328
00:22:48,451 --> 00:22:50,161
Go ahead, Mr. Salvador.

329
00:22:55,833 --> 00:22:57,210
Before anything else,

330
00:22:57,210 --> 00:23:01,839
I want you to remember
what Diana stood for.

331
00:23:03,049 --> 00:23:05,510
And I want you to choose

332
00:23:05,510 --> 00:23:09,639
what would be best
for La Familia.

333
00:23:09,639 --> 00:23:11,808
Its future...

334
00:23:14,102 --> 00:23:17,188
- ...is in your hands.
- Wait!

335
00:23:17,188 --> 00:23:18,856
- Let us in!
- Sir! Ma'am!

336
00:23:18,856 --> 00:23:21,359
- The doors are already closed!
- No, let us in!

337
00:23:21,359 --> 00:23:23,611
- Step aside.
- You can't come in.

338
00:23:23,611 --> 00:23:25,029
- Says who?
- Out of the way.

339
00:23:25,029 --> 00:23:26,697
- Sorry, but--
- Let us in, or else...

340
00:23:26,697 --> 00:23:28,241
I'm here.

341
00:23:28,241 --> 00:23:30,201
We can start voting now.

342
00:23:52,682 --> 00:23:53,683
Wait.

343
00:23:58,020 --> 00:24:01,149
Georgia Aragon is here
as her father's proxy.

344
00:24:02,817 --> 00:24:04,986
The documents are in order, sir.

345
00:24:07,196 --> 00:24:08,656
We can now start the voting.

346
00:24:47,403 --> 00:24:49,197
By resolution of the board,

347
00:24:49,989 --> 00:24:52,158
it is hereby declared

348
00:24:52,158 --> 00:24:57,538
that the new president and
chief executive officer is...

349
00:25:03,502 --> 00:25:06,631
Mr. Ricardo Salvador!

350
00:25:37,161 --> 00:25:39,163
I brought
a special guest for you.

351
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:44,585
- Daddy?
- Georgia?

352
00:25:44,585 --> 00:25:45,670
Dad!

353
00:25:45,670 --> 00:25:47,213
Georgia!

354
00:25:47,213 --> 00:25:48,547
Are you okay?

355
00:25:48,547 --> 00:25:50,466
Are you hurt?
Did he hurt you?

356
00:25:50,466 --> 00:25:52,176
- Dad!
- Dear...

357
00:25:52,176 --> 00:25:53,678
You monster!

358
00:25:53,678 --> 00:25:55,888
Why get my daughter involved?
What else do you want?!

359
00:26:01,477 --> 00:26:03,562
You will do everything I say.

360
00:26:04,730 --> 00:26:08,276
Otherwise, your daughter
will suffer like you.

361
00:26:12,947 --> 00:26:15,324
- Congratulations.
- Thank you for your support.

362
00:26:15,324 --> 00:26:16,575
Yeah, yeah.

363
00:26:16,575 --> 00:26:19,537
- I'll be seeing you.
- Yeah.

364
00:26:19,537 --> 00:26:21,455
It seems someone's unhappy.

365
00:26:23,582 --> 00:26:25,167
- I'll talk to her.
- Okay.

366
00:26:30,047 --> 00:26:31,132
Patricia.

367
00:26:35,803 --> 00:26:38,597
And you say
your intentions are pure?

368
00:26:39,598 --> 00:26:42,018
I'm just thinking
about La Familia's future

369
00:26:43,352 --> 00:26:45,688
and what the company deserves.

370
00:26:45,688 --> 00:26:47,815
Maybe they thought
you aren't ready to lead.

371
00:26:47,815 --> 00:26:49,233
And you can?

372
00:26:51,777 --> 00:26:55,281
You're nothing compared
to my mother.

373
00:26:56,907 --> 00:26:59,118
You haven't seen my worst.

374
00:27:01,662 --> 00:27:05,499
I can be ruthless
when someone hurts my family.

375
00:27:07,501 --> 00:27:08,961
First, it was Mama.

376
00:27:10,379 --> 00:27:12,131
Now, you're also targeting Papa.

377
00:27:13,841 --> 00:27:16,469
You shouldn't have dragged
Papa into this!

378
00:27:17,928 --> 00:27:21,098
First of all, I didn't do
anything wrong to your mother.

379
00:27:21,098 --> 00:27:24,602
And more importantly, I have
nothing to do with your father.

380
00:27:25,728 --> 00:27:29,398
But you sent men to our house.
For what?

381
00:27:29,398 --> 00:27:32,568
Patricia, why do you
keep accusing me?

382
00:27:33,569 --> 00:27:35,196
You know your father.

383
00:27:35,946 --> 00:27:38,324
He has a lot of enemies.

384
00:27:40,493 --> 00:27:42,328
I think you're being unfair.

385
00:27:42,912 --> 00:27:45,081
Nothing's fair about
what's happening here.

386
00:27:49,919 --> 00:27:51,379
You think you've won?

387
00:27:52,838 --> 00:27:55,299
I won't make your life easy.

388
00:27:56,967 --> 00:28:01,097
No matter how much you try
to bury the truth,

389
00:28:01,097 --> 00:28:03,099
no secret remains
hidden forever.

390
00:28:03,099 --> 00:28:04,308
Well...

391
00:28:04,809 --> 00:28:06,060
you're right.

392
00:28:09,021 --> 00:28:11,899
But how will you
unearth the truth

393
00:28:13,067 --> 00:28:15,403
if you have no power
to do so?

394
00:28:16,862 --> 00:28:17,988
Hey.

395
00:28:18,697 --> 00:28:20,157
I'm sorry, I have to go.

396
00:28:22,076 --> 00:28:23,494
Take care.

397
00:28:31,627 --> 00:28:35,047
I've done what you want.
Now, let Daddy go.

398
00:28:38,384 --> 00:28:40,344
When did I agree to do that?

399
00:28:42,179 --> 00:28:43,639
That's not fair!

400
00:28:45,307 --> 00:28:47,268
I did what you asked!

401
00:28:51,439 --> 00:28:52,898
Georgia...

402
00:28:54,608 --> 00:28:56,819
It's not my fault
if you're naive.

403
00:28:57,903 --> 00:28:59,655
Did you honestly think

404
00:28:59,655 --> 00:29:02,616
that I'd let someone who
knows too much run free?

405
00:29:03,451 --> 00:29:05,703
Someone who has
no sense of loyalty?

406
00:29:06,787 --> 00:29:09,290
He betrayed his own sister.

407
00:29:11,250 --> 00:29:13,210
He can do the same to me.

408
00:29:13,210 --> 00:29:14,670
You monster...

409
00:29:14,670 --> 00:29:16,422
You filthy monster!

410
00:29:16,422 --> 00:29:19,008
You just used me!

411
00:29:19,008 --> 00:29:21,760
What makes you think
I'll keep my mouth shut?

412
00:29:21,760 --> 00:29:24,638
I'll tell Patricia
everything you made me do!

413
00:29:26,891 --> 00:29:28,225
Just you try.

414
00:29:32,980 --> 00:29:34,690
That's if...

415
00:29:36,358 --> 00:29:39,320
...you want your father to
lose all chances of living.

416
00:30:06,013 --> 00:30:07,139
Who is this?

417
00:30:07,139 --> 00:30:09,016
This is Sandra, my secretary.

418
00:30:09,850 --> 00:30:11,560
She'll be staying here
for the time being.

419
00:30:13,187 --> 00:30:18,359
I don't think it's appropriate
for her to stay here.

420
00:30:19,527 --> 00:30:22,029
Did I ask for your opinion,
Nanny Cora?

421
00:30:22,029 --> 00:30:23,989
Hmm?
What's your place here?

422
00:30:25,032 --> 00:30:26,825
You're a maid.

423
00:30:26,825 --> 00:30:29,328
I don't need your approval.

424
00:30:29,328 --> 00:30:31,539
Yes, I'm just a maid.

425
00:30:32,456 --> 00:30:34,416
I'm not a blood relative.

426
00:30:35,876 --> 00:30:39,588
But for Diana and Patricia,

427
00:30:40,297 --> 00:30:42,007
I am their family.

428
00:30:42,007 --> 00:30:44,301
I am like a mother to them.

429
00:30:44,301 --> 00:30:50,558
They love, respect,
and care for me like one.

430
00:30:51,433 --> 00:30:53,269
And as their mother,

431
00:30:53,269 --> 00:30:55,813
I will do everything
in my power

432
00:30:55,813 --> 00:30:57,648
to protect them

433
00:30:57,648 --> 00:31:01,819
from anyone
who may bring them harm.

434
00:31:03,070 --> 00:31:06,073
Wow, the help here
is so dramatic.

435
00:31:06,073 --> 00:31:09,368
Whatever, Cora.
Just prepare us some food.

436
00:31:09,368 --> 00:31:10,995
And watch it, all right?

437
00:31:11,912 --> 00:31:13,289
What are you waiting for?

438
00:31:29,972 --> 00:31:31,056
Hello?

439
00:32:34,662 --> 00:32:35,871
Dad?

440
00:32:35,871 --> 00:32:37,122
Daddy.

441
00:32:37,122 --> 00:32:38,957
Daddy, wake up.
Wake up.

442
00:32:38,957 --> 00:32:40,459
- Georgia, why are you here?
- I'm getting you out of here.

443
00:32:40,459 --> 00:32:42,628
We're getting out of here.
Okay?

444
00:32:42,628 --> 00:32:44,296
- We need the key.
- What?

445
00:32:44,296 --> 00:32:46,882
- We need the key.
- Shh!

446
00:32:46,882 --> 00:32:48,759
- We have to go!
- It's not safe, Georgia.

447
00:32:48,759 --> 00:32:50,427
We have to go!

448
00:32:50,427 --> 00:32:51,553
No! No! No!
Georgia!

449
00:32:51,553 --> 00:32:52,596
You bastard!

450
00:32:52,596 --> 00:32:54,098
Georgia! Georgia...

451
00:32:54,098 --> 00:32:55,599
Georgia...
Wake up, Georgia!

452
00:32:55,599 --> 00:32:57,142
Georgia! Georgia!

453
00:32:58,560 --> 00:33:03,148
Michelle, tell Cora
to fetch my suit and bag.

454
00:33:03,148 --> 00:33:04,900
I'll do it, sir.

455
00:33:05,901 --> 00:33:07,361
Why? Where is Nanny Cora?

456
00:33:07,361 --> 00:33:08,987
We don't know, sir.

457
00:33:08,987 --> 00:33:10,698
What do you mean
you don't know?

458
00:33:10,698 --> 00:33:13,826
She wasn't here
when we woke up.

459
00:33:13,826 --> 00:33:15,828
All her belongings are gone too.

460
00:33:37,057 --> 00:33:38,726
I'm here.

461
00:33:51,739 --> 00:33:52,740
Dad?

462
00:33:55,451 --> 00:33:56,535
Dad?

463
00:33:57,453 --> 00:33:58,579
Dad?

464
00:34:00,539 --> 00:34:01,665
Daddy?

465
00:34:02,332 --> 00:34:03,500
Daddy...

466
00:34:05,794 --> 00:34:06,920
Daddy.

467
00:34:08,881 --> 00:34:11,467
Daddy!

468
00:34:12,843 --> 00:34:14,553
The subscriber
cannot be reached.

469
00:34:14,553 --> 00:34:16,847
I still can't reach Georgia.

470
00:34:17,639 --> 00:34:19,767
Georgia? Georgia!

471
00:34:19,767 --> 00:34:22,102
Hey, what happened?

472
00:34:22,102 --> 00:34:24,062
I tried to save Dad.

473
00:34:24,897 --> 00:34:26,190
What?

474
00:34:26,190 --> 00:34:28,275
But I failed.

475
00:34:28,275 --> 00:34:32,404
Wait, Georgia, maybe we should
take you to the hospital.

476
00:34:32,404 --> 00:34:35,240
Patricia, I found him.

477
00:34:35,240 --> 00:34:36,992
We were together again.

478
00:34:36,992 --> 00:34:38,994
We were going to escape.

479
00:34:38,994 --> 00:34:41,246
But when I woke up,
he was gone.

480
00:34:41,246 --> 00:34:45,292
I tried to find him,
but he was gone!

481
00:34:45,292 --> 00:34:48,670
I don't know where
they took my dad!

482
00:34:51,048 --> 00:34:53,258
This is all Ricardo's fault.

483
00:34:54,802 --> 00:34:56,220
Georgia, wait.

484
00:34:56,220 --> 00:34:57,346
Georgia!

485
00:34:57,346 --> 00:35:00,474
I don't have any information
about Nanny Cora yet.

486
00:35:02,017 --> 00:35:05,687
I might know someone
who knows where she is.

487
00:35:05,687 --> 00:35:07,022
Is it Patricia?

488
00:35:07,773 --> 00:35:09,566
Nanny Cora is missing.

489
00:35:11,026 --> 00:35:12,861
And she has never...

490
00:35:14,530 --> 00:35:16,573
...been away from Diana.

491
00:35:19,368 --> 00:35:21,078
Where did you take my dad?

492
00:35:21,078 --> 00:35:22,246
Tell me!

493
00:35:23,497 --> 00:35:26,959
You made me do things
against my will.

494
00:35:26,959 --> 00:35:29,253
You tortured my dad to
force him to do as you say.

495
00:35:29,253 --> 00:35:31,296
And now you've
taken him again?

496
00:35:32,673 --> 00:35:34,091
Answer Georgia.

497
00:35:34,842 --> 00:35:36,802
Do you really believe this girl?

498
00:35:36,802 --> 00:35:39,096
She's hated you ever since.

499
00:35:40,180 --> 00:35:42,391
She and her father
are the same.

500
00:35:42,391 --> 00:35:43,934
They'll make up stories

501
00:35:43,934 --> 00:35:46,353
just to save themselves.

502
00:35:47,145 --> 00:35:49,314
Have you forgotten
about that, Patricia?

503
00:35:50,065 --> 00:35:52,734
I'm not the kind of person
who forgets easily.

504
00:35:52,734 --> 00:35:55,612
I never forget anyone
who crosses me.

505
00:35:56,321 --> 00:35:59,283
Especially those who lie to me
and play me for a fool.

506
00:36:00,742 --> 00:36:04,204
So I know
who is telling the truth

507
00:36:04,204 --> 00:36:05,706
and who is lying.

508
00:36:07,291 --> 00:36:08,709
And most importantly,

509
00:36:09,626 --> 00:36:12,129
no matter what happened
in the past,

510
00:36:15,674 --> 00:36:17,467
we're family.

511
00:36:17,467 --> 00:36:19,845
We're Aragons.

512
00:36:19,845 --> 00:36:22,180
You're crossing the line,
Patricia.

513
00:36:22,931 --> 00:36:27,853
Who are you to speak
to the CEO like that?

514
00:36:28,645 --> 00:36:31,690
You seem to have forgotten
how to show respect.

515
00:36:31,690 --> 00:36:33,650
Oh...

516
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:36,361
Don't lecture me about respect.

517
00:36:36,361 --> 00:36:38,864
You should be ashamed
of yourself!

518
00:36:40,991 --> 00:36:43,076
My mother just died.

519
00:36:44,536 --> 00:36:48,582
How dare you bring your
ex-wife into our home!

520
00:36:48,582 --> 00:36:50,834
Don't you have
a shred of decency left?!

521
00:36:50,834 --> 00:36:52,210
Patricia!

522
00:36:52,210 --> 00:36:53,587
Georgia!

523
00:36:53,587 --> 00:36:55,380
Enough.

524
00:36:57,507 --> 00:36:59,051
Georgia, let's go.

525
00:37:08,852 --> 00:37:10,812
- Enzo...
- Sir.

526
00:37:11,647 --> 00:37:13,023
Tell me the truth.

527
00:37:15,150 --> 00:37:16,944
Are we still on the same side?

528
00:37:17,986 --> 00:37:19,863
My decision hasn't changed.

529
00:37:23,784 --> 00:37:25,577
Are you sure?

530
00:37:25,577 --> 00:37:28,830
I need justice for my parents.

531
00:37:29,623 --> 00:37:31,541
You have no reason
to doubt me.

532
00:37:33,418 --> 00:37:35,212
What is Patricia's plan?

533
00:37:36,546 --> 00:37:39,549
She's still preparing
to take you down.

534
00:37:39,549 --> 00:37:43,303
She will do everything
to get rid of you.

535
00:37:44,930 --> 00:37:46,306
And how will she do that?

536
00:37:46,306 --> 00:37:47,975
I'm still trying to find out.

537
00:37:47,975 --> 00:37:50,310
Patricia has become secretive.

538
00:37:51,061 --> 00:37:53,981
But I assume she doesn't know
what to do yet.

539
00:37:53,981 --> 00:37:57,693
As soon as I find out,
I'll inform you right away.

540
00:37:58,652 --> 00:38:02,239
But their priority right now
is finding Sir Teddy.

541
00:38:02,906 --> 00:38:05,826
They think you're the one
who took him.

542
00:38:06,535 --> 00:38:07,911
Are they right?

543
00:38:10,622 --> 00:38:14,334
I'm not convinced
I can trust you yet.

544
00:38:16,461 --> 00:38:18,755
You have to prove
yourself to me.

545
00:38:19,423 --> 00:38:21,133
For now,

546
00:38:21,133 --> 00:38:24,386
find out
what Patricia's planning.

547
00:38:25,220 --> 00:38:27,472
And get back to me right away.

548
00:38:37,983 --> 00:38:40,986
How does Patricia know
I'm your ex-wife?

549
00:38:41,862 --> 00:38:44,114
Diana was the only one
who knew about that.

550
00:38:48,452 --> 00:38:52,831
What do you think will happen
now that Sir Ricardo is CEO?

551
00:38:53,832 --> 00:38:55,167
I don't want to know.

552
00:38:55,167 --> 00:38:56,877
I'm scared.

553
00:38:56,877 --> 00:38:58,670
Same here.

554
00:38:58,670 --> 00:39:01,506
I'm getting a bad vibe
from him.

555
00:39:01,506 --> 00:39:02,841
Oh, by the way.

556
00:39:02,841 --> 00:39:04,301
Have you seen this?

557
00:39:04,301 --> 00:39:06,970
- Did you read the memo?
- What does it say?

558
00:39:06,970 --> 00:39:10,640
There's an out-of-town
stockholders' summit.

559
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:13,060
The details were sent via email.

560
00:39:14,686 --> 00:39:16,855
- Let me see.
- Sure.

561
00:39:19,691 --> 00:39:20,901
Hmm...

562
00:39:28,075 --> 00:39:32,245
I take it you've read about
the stockholders' summit.

563
00:39:32,245 --> 00:39:34,581
Sir, what is this for?

564
00:39:36,541 --> 00:39:40,170
Lala, please explain
what this event is to Patricia.

565
00:39:40,170 --> 00:39:41,797
I know what the event is.

566
00:39:41,797 --> 00:39:44,925
My question is,
what is it really for?

567
00:39:46,843 --> 00:39:48,220
Why don't you come?

568
00:39:49,179 --> 00:39:50,639
See it for yourself.

569
00:39:50,639 --> 00:39:52,182
Oh, I'll go.

570
00:39:52,974 --> 00:39:54,935
I won't miss it.

571
00:40:13,620 --> 00:40:15,372
Eat!

572
00:40:20,043 --> 00:40:21,503
How will I eat

573
00:40:23,922 --> 00:40:25,382
if my hands are tied?

574
00:40:42,065 --> 00:40:49,114
Aah! Aah!

575
00:40:59,541 --> 00:41:01,042
Argh!

576
00:41:28,904 --> 00:41:30,238
Mrs. Smith.

577
00:41:32,908 --> 00:41:36,203
I heard you're bringing
Patricia along

578
00:41:36,203 --> 00:41:38,288
to the shareholders' summit.

579
00:41:38,288 --> 00:41:40,957
I just want them to see
that Patricia has no

580
00:41:40,957 --> 00:41:42,792
being part of La Familia.

581
00:41:43,627 --> 00:41:45,921
You're just looking
for a headache.

582
00:41:45,921 --> 00:41:49,507
She's going to question
your decisions there.

583
00:41:50,467 --> 00:41:52,010
Carlota,

584
00:41:52,010 --> 00:41:55,096
you and Mr. Smith
just acquired shares.

585
00:41:56,681 --> 00:41:59,267
But you don't call the shots.

586
00:41:59,809 --> 00:42:01,478
I know what I'm doing.

587
00:42:02,479 --> 00:42:03,772
I don't want

588
00:42:04,439 --> 00:42:07,108
Patricia there.

589
00:42:08,401 --> 00:42:09,653
I know.

590
00:42:10,487 --> 00:42:12,739
Why don't we just work together

591
00:42:14,407 --> 00:42:16,618
to get Patricia
out of the company?

592
00:42:30,131 --> 00:42:32,217
We can't
expose Ricardo yet

593
00:42:32,217 --> 00:42:34,177
as long as Uncle Teddy
is in his hands.

594
00:42:36,346 --> 00:42:38,640
I'm really scared.

595
00:42:38,640 --> 00:42:41,226
They might have done
something to Dad.

596
00:42:41,226 --> 00:42:43,478
I might never see him again.

597
00:42:48,775 --> 00:42:50,443
Georgia... Georgia...

598
00:42:52,445 --> 00:42:53,655
Calm down.

599
00:42:54,531 --> 00:42:55,949
Don't think like that.

600
00:42:56,658 --> 00:42:58,660
We'll find a way to figure out

601
00:42:58,660 --> 00:43:01,121
where he's being kept.

602
00:43:03,707 --> 00:43:06,209
The information Enzo
gathered isn't enough yet.

603
00:43:06,835 --> 00:43:08,878
They don't fully trust me yet.

604
00:43:09,796 --> 00:43:11,131
That's why I can't get a lead

605
00:43:11,131 --> 00:43:13,091
on where they might be hiding
Sir Teddy.

606
00:43:15,051 --> 00:43:16,344
But I think...

607
00:43:16,344 --> 00:43:17,846
Sandra might know something.

608
00:43:18,263 --> 00:43:19,764
Why her?

609
00:43:19,764 --> 00:43:22,809
Because they're always together
and they're always talking.

610
00:43:23,310 --> 00:43:26,271
And whenever they talk,
they ask me to leave the room.

611
00:43:27,147 --> 00:43:29,816
There are things that
Sir Ricardo only tells her.

612
00:43:30,859 --> 00:43:31,943
That's possible.

613
00:43:33,820 --> 00:43:36,364
But we also need
to look at other angles.

614
00:43:37,449 --> 00:43:39,117
Ricardo is too cunning.

615
00:43:40,201 --> 00:43:41,828
What's your plan, Patricia?

616
00:43:42,495 --> 00:43:44,956
Don't worry.
I'm coming up with a plan.

617
00:43:48,126 --> 00:43:49,419
Patricia.

618
00:43:51,588 --> 00:43:52,547
Pa.

619
00:43:53,048 --> 00:43:54,299
- Enzo.
- Sir.

620
00:43:56,885 --> 00:43:58,178
Oh.

621
00:43:58,595 --> 00:44:00,347
I didn't know you had a visitor.

622
00:44:00,930 --> 00:44:02,265
Yes, uh...

623
00:44:02,265 --> 00:44:04,601
We're talking about
what to do on the summit.

624
00:44:05,352 --> 00:44:06,478
Have you eaten yet?

625
00:44:06,478 --> 00:44:08,146
- I'll prepare your food.
- I'll help you.

626
00:44:08,146 --> 00:44:09,356
Where's the bathroom?

627
00:44:09,356 --> 00:44:10,690
Right there.

628
00:44:27,874 --> 00:44:29,459
Hello?

629
00:44:29,459 --> 00:44:32,128
You guys aren't being careful!
You aren't thinking!

630
00:44:32,504 --> 00:44:34,339
You know that guy
is a troublemaker!

631
00:44:34,339 --> 00:44:36,174
Yes! I'm on my way.

632
00:44:41,096 --> 00:44:42,847
Ma'am, here's what
you asked me to buy.

633
00:44:42,847 --> 00:44:45,225
That was the only bakery
close to that place.

634
00:45:19,676 --> 00:45:20,844
Hello?

635
00:45:21,719 --> 00:45:23,179
Yes, I'm on my way!

636
00:45:41,906 --> 00:45:43,283
Where's Patricia?

637
00:45:43,950 --> 00:45:45,201
She's coming here, sir.

638
00:45:45,785 --> 00:45:46,995
Why is she coming?

639
00:45:48,371 --> 00:45:50,999
She said she'll tell me
when we meet later.

640
00:45:52,625 --> 00:45:54,002
Where was she the other day?

641
00:45:55,462 --> 00:45:57,255
She said she was going
to see her father, sir.

642
00:45:58,047 --> 00:45:59,466
She didn't ask you to come?

643
00:46:05,305 --> 00:46:07,307
Lately, she hasn't been
opening up to me much.

644
00:46:08,016 --> 00:46:09,809
I need you
to do something.

645
00:46:10,560 --> 00:46:11,936
Anything, sir.

646
00:46:12,604 --> 00:46:15,231
Patricia can't make it
to the summit.

647
00:46:17,484 --> 00:46:19,736
Do whatever it takes
to stop her from getting there.

648
00:46:20,695 --> 00:46:21,905
Do you understand?

649
00:46:23,239 --> 00:46:24,324
How?

650
00:46:24,324 --> 00:46:25,783
You're smart, aren't you?!

651
00:46:26,326 --> 00:46:27,577
Figure it out!

652
00:46:28,119 --> 00:46:29,370
Find a way!

653
00:46:29,996 --> 00:46:31,915
As long as she isn't
at the summit!

654
00:46:35,376 --> 00:46:37,795
I know Patricia is
plotting against me.

655
00:46:46,679 --> 00:46:49,516
What do you want
to talk about, Patricia?

656
00:46:49,516 --> 00:46:53,186
You are the longest-serving
board members in the company.

657
00:46:53,895 --> 00:46:55,605
You started around
the same time as Mama,

658
00:46:55,605 --> 00:46:59,275
and I know you became close
to each other.

659
00:46:59,776 --> 00:47:02,445
And you saw how Mama
handled the company.

660
00:47:02,445 --> 00:47:04,697
I know you trust her deeply.

661
00:47:05,114 --> 00:47:07,367
Where is
this conversation going?

662
00:47:07,367 --> 00:47:09,327
My only request is...

663
00:47:10,245 --> 00:47:13,665
that you please be careful
with every decision you make.

664
00:47:16,125 --> 00:47:17,627
What are you trying to say?

665
00:47:18,169 --> 00:47:20,547
Someone wants to
bring down La Familia.

666
00:47:24,300 --> 00:47:25,635
So, please...

667
00:47:26,052 --> 00:47:27,887
no matter what happens,

668
00:47:29,097 --> 00:47:35,144
remember what Mama fought for
at La Familia all these years.

669
00:47:36,354 --> 00:47:37,897
For the company

670
00:47:37,897 --> 00:47:40,191
that has also become
a huge part of your lives.

671
00:47:41,985 --> 00:47:43,945
She built La Familia up

672
00:47:43,945 --> 00:47:47,365
for the so many people
who depend on it,

673
00:47:48,157 --> 00:47:50,285
and you are some
of those people.

674
00:47:51,286 --> 00:47:52,620
So I hope...

675
00:47:53,454 --> 00:47:54,956
you'll help me,

676
00:47:56,791 --> 00:47:58,668
you'll help me make sure

677
00:47:58,668 --> 00:48:01,087
everything she worked hard
for isn't lost.

678
00:48:05,675 --> 00:48:06,884
Patricia.

679
00:48:08,136 --> 00:48:10,388
Enzo, what's going on?

680
00:48:10,805 --> 00:48:12,056
You were right.

681
00:48:13,349 --> 00:48:14,726
He wants to stop you.

682
00:48:23,985 --> 00:48:26,237
- If you ever need anything--
- I'm leaving, Pa.

683
00:48:26,237 --> 00:48:27,405
Patricia.

684
00:48:27,905 --> 00:48:29,073
Thank you.

685
00:48:29,073 --> 00:48:30,617
I'm coming with you.

686
00:48:30,617 --> 00:48:33,036
Don't worry. I'm with Enzo.

687
00:48:34,037 --> 00:48:35,246
Good morning, sir.

688
00:48:35,830 --> 00:48:37,498
Patricia, let's go?

689
00:48:38,625 --> 00:48:39,667
Bye.

690
00:48:40,710 --> 00:48:41,753
Dear.

691
00:48:45,590 --> 00:48:47,467
Take care, okay?

692
00:48:48,760 --> 00:48:49,927
Enzo?

693
00:48:50,762 --> 00:48:52,555
Watch out for each other.

694
00:48:52,555 --> 00:48:53,640
Yes.

695
00:48:56,517 --> 00:48:57,977
I love you, Pa.

696
00:49:06,944 --> 00:49:08,571
- Go.
- Okay.

697
00:49:08,571 --> 00:49:10,031
Be careful, okay?

698
00:49:28,132 --> 00:49:29,425
They're here.

699
00:49:30,802 --> 00:49:32,679
- Good morning, Mr. Smith.
- Good morning.

700
00:49:50,405 --> 00:49:51,864
Good morning, Ma'am Carlota.

701
00:49:51,864 --> 00:49:53,825
Welcome to La Familia
Shareholder Summit.

702
00:49:55,493 --> 00:49:56,994
Ma'am, can you
give us an update

703
00:49:56,994 --> 00:49:58,996
- about the summit today?
- Please, please, please.

704
00:50:00,081 --> 00:50:02,417
Let's go. They're ready
in the function room.

705
00:50:03,334 --> 00:50:04,502
Good luck.

706
00:50:13,010 --> 00:50:14,095
Sir Ricardo.

707
00:50:14,095 --> 00:50:15,388
Did you get it done?

708
00:50:15,388 --> 00:50:16,389
Yes, sir.

709
00:50:17,640 --> 00:50:19,183
Patricia's in the hospital.

710
00:50:21,561 --> 00:50:22,729
Let me see her.

711
00:50:33,656 --> 00:50:34,824
Very good!

712
00:50:37,452 --> 00:50:39,078
Let's go?
They're getting started.

713
00:50:49,630 --> 00:50:52,550
Enzo, the building
we're going to,

714
00:50:53,426 --> 00:50:54,886
are you sure about it?

715
00:50:55,344 --> 00:50:57,096
I looked for that bakeshop.

716
00:50:58,139 --> 00:51:01,476
I have a strong feeling
Sir Teddy is nearby.

717
00:51:02,769 --> 00:51:04,604
We have to get there now.

718
00:51:10,818 --> 00:51:13,154
So, where
do we start looking?

719
00:51:17,408 --> 00:51:20,244
That's the name of the bakeshop
Sandra's henchman gave her.

720
00:51:31,380 --> 00:51:32,924
Come on, let's follow him.

721
00:52:08,417 --> 00:52:10,211
Here. Eat up.

722
00:52:10,211 --> 00:52:11,796
Use your mouth
to scoop up your food.

723
00:52:16,717 --> 00:52:17,718
Hey!

724
00:52:17,718 --> 00:52:18,761
Teddy!

725
00:52:19,512 --> 00:52:20,555
Hey!

726
00:52:20,555 --> 00:52:21,514
Hey!

727
00:52:21,514 --> 00:52:22,598
Teddy!

728
00:52:22,598 --> 00:52:23,599
Hey!

729
00:53:18,487 --> 00:53:19,697
Teddy!

730
00:53:19,697 --> 00:53:21,449
Teddy!

731
00:53:26,412 --> 00:53:27,622
That's Daddy.

732
00:53:42,219 --> 00:53:43,346
Hold on.

733
00:53:50,353 --> 00:53:52,021
What happened to you?!

734
00:53:52,021 --> 00:53:53,272
He escaped!

735
00:53:55,650 --> 00:53:57,568
Let's look for him.
He can't have gone far.

736
00:54:03,574 --> 00:54:05,076
He escaped?

737
00:54:20,758 --> 00:54:23,511
Let's find him
before they get to him first.

738
00:54:23,928 --> 00:54:27,056
Let's split up
so we can find him faster.

739
00:54:27,056 --> 00:54:28,933
Patricia,
that's too dangerous.

740
00:54:28,933 --> 00:54:30,726
I can take care
of myself, Enzo.

741
00:55:16,731 --> 00:55:19,442
To mark the change
in the board of La Familia,

742
00:55:20,067 --> 00:55:22,611
I want the public to be part

743
00:55:22,987 --> 00:55:25,072
of the company's new direction.

744
00:55:25,906 --> 00:55:30,578
A celebration
of La Familia's new life.

745
00:55:40,755 --> 00:55:43,799
So, I asked
the product development team,

746
00:55:43,799 --> 00:55:46,135
closely supervised by me,

747
00:55:46,135 --> 00:55:48,971
to create an improved product.

748
00:55:52,475 --> 00:55:53,934
Ladies and gentlemen,

749
00:55:54,602 --> 00:55:57,063
the new Cala Soda.

750
00:55:59,023 --> 00:56:00,316
Reformulated.

751
00:56:02,193 --> 00:56:04,195
Revitalized.

752
00:56:04,195 --> 00:56:09,950
It symbolizes our move toward
a new future for La Familia.

753
00:56:11,994 --> 00:56:13,329
Along with this,

754
00:56:14,121 --> 00:56:19,543
we will also unveil
La Familia's new logo.

755
00:56:23,464 --> 00:56:25,841
However, it's not just
our products and branding

756
00:56:25,841 --> 00:56:27,384
that need to change.

757
00:56:27,885 --> 00:56:31,430
To keep La Familia's operations
running smoothly,

758
00:56:31,430 --> 00:56:34,433
we also need to restructure.

759
00:56:34,975 --> 00:56:36,560
And sad to say,

760
00:56:38,145 --> 00:56:40,231
this restructuring
will also mean

761
00:56:41,148 --> 00:56:43,609
laying off some employees.

762
00:56:51,033 --> 00:56:52,785
Yes, Mr. Vega?

763
00:56:52,785 --> 00:56:54,370
Is it right for us
to be discussing

764
00:56:54,370 --> 00:56:56,080
these kinds of things?

765
00:56:56,080 --> 00:56:59,792
One of our major shareholders
isn't even here yet.

766
00:56:59,792 --> 00:57:01,961
By the way, why isn't
Patricia here?

767
00:57:01,961 --> 00:57:04,630
I'm sure she has lots
of thoughts about this.

768
00:57:04,630 --> 00:57:05,840
Mr. Vega,

769
00:57:06,423 --> 00:57:07,883
change is inevitable.

770
00:57:07,883 --> 00:57:09,301
After a thorough analysis,

771
00:57:09,301 --> 00:57:11,595
I've thought this is what's best
for the company.

772
00:57:12,263 --> 00:57:13,681
Ricardo,

773
00:57:13,681 --> 00:57:16,642
this isn't something
you should just think about.

774
00:57:16,642 --> 00:57:19,812
With your decisions,
it's as if you're saying...

775
00:57:19,812 --> 00:57:24,733
you want to erase something
that built La Familia.

776
00:57:24,733 --> 00:57:27,236
What about
the Aragon family's legacy?

777
00:57:28,529 --> 00:57:30,823
I'm doing this because
I'm thinking about

778
00:57:30,823 --> 00:57:32,700
La Familia's legacy.

779
00:57:34,201 --> 00:57:35,911
What legacy will we have
to talk about

780
00:57:35,911 --> 00:57:37,413
if the company goes bankrupt?

781
00:57:39,081 --> 00:57:41,041
Why don't we put it to a vote?

782
00:57:41,500 --> 00:57:42,835
Patricia isn't here,

783
00:57:43,419 --> 00:57:45,379
our major shareholder.

784
00:57:45,379 --> 00:57:48,299
Mr. Meneses, all the
shareholders are here.

785
00:57:48,299 --> 00:57:49,800
All the board members are here.

786
00:57:51,010 --> 00:57:54,430
No one can say we can't vote
just because of one person.

787
00:57:54,430 --> 00:57:56,640
I agree
with Mr. Salvador.

788
00:57:56,640 --> 00:57:59,143
Those in favor of the
proposed change,

789
00:57:59,143 --> 00:58:00,603
raise your hands.

790
00:58:08,569 --> 00:58:11,405
You have a problem
with this, my love? Hmm?

791
00:58:17,453 --> 00:58:18,996
The majority has spoken.

792
00:58:30,090 --> 00:58:33,469
Following the controversial
death of Diana Aragon,

793
00:58:33,469 --> 00:58:36,222
Ricardo Salvador
was officially named

794
00:58:36,222 --> 00:58:38,849
the new CEO of La Familia.

795
00:58:38,849 --> 00:58:41,310
With the support
of the board members,

796
00:58:41,310 --> 00:58:43,270
the new leadership
assured the public

797
00:58:43,270 --> 00:58:45,272
that they would
restore stability

798
00:58:45,272 --> 00:58:47,775
and the corporation's
public trust.

799
00:58:58,911 --> 00:59:00,329
I'll end La Familia,

800
00:59:00,329 --> 00:59:01,914
and there's nothing Patricia
can do about it.

801
00:59:01,914 --> 00:59:03,374
What happened?!

802
00:59:03,374 --> 00:59:07,503
That fire is the root
of all this!

803
00:59:07,503 --> 00:59:12,466
I will do everything to reclaim
my mother's company.

804
00:59:12,466 --> 00:59:13,592
Diana?

805
00:59:13,592 --> 00:59:15,552
- Diana!
- What are you saying?

806
00:59:15,552 --> 00:59:16,679
I saw Diana!

807
00:59:16,679 --> 00:59:18,264
Drop the act.

808
00:59:18,264 --> 00:59:21,642
You think I'll let
all my hard work go to waste?!

809
00:59:21,642 --> 00:59:23,310
You'll all pay for this!

810
00:59:23,310 --> 00:59:24,853
That's enough, Ricardo!
